for expressive interactive ensemble music performance.\n911\t\n912\tIn Proceedings of the 16th International Society for Music Information Retrieval Conference,\n913\t\n914\t pp. 816–822.\n915\t\n916\tCited by: §1.\n917\t\n918\t- \n919\t[35]\n920\tY. Yang, Z. Jin, C. Barnes, and A. Finkelstein (2023)\n921\t\n922\tWhite box search over audio synthesizer parameters.\n923\t\n924\tIn Proceedings of the 24th International Society for Music Information Retrieval Conference,\n925\t\n926\t pp. 190–196.\n927\t\n928\tCited by: §1,\n929\t§2.1.\n930\t\n931\t- \n932\t[36]\n933\tX. Yi, Q. He, G. Xia, and Z. Wang (2026)\n934\t\n935\tViTex: visual texture control for multi-track symbolic music generation via discrete diffusion models.\n936\t\n937\tarXiv preprint arXiv:2603.01984.\n938\t\n939\tCited by: §2.2.\n940\t\n941\t- \n942\t[37]\n943\tR. Yuan, H. Lin, Y. Wang, Z. Tian, S. Wu, T. Shen, G. Zhang, Y. Wu, C. Liu, Z. Zhou, et al. (2024)\n944\t\n945\tChatMusician: understanding and generating music intrinsically with LLM.\n946\t\n947\tIn Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: ACL 2024,\n948\t\n949\t pp. 6252–6271.\n950\t\n951\tCited by: §1.\n952\t\n953\t- \n954\t[38]\n955\tS. Zhao, D. Gupta, Q. Zheng, and A. Grover (2025)\n956\t\n957\td1: scaling reasoning in diffusion large language models via reinforcement learning.\n958\t\n959\tIn Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems,\n960\t\n961\tVol. 38, pp. 56729–56762.\n962\t\n963\tCited by: §2.3.\n964\t\n965\t Experimental support, please\n966\t view the build logs\n967\t for errors. Generated by\n968\t\n969\t L\n970\t A\n971\t T\n972\t E\n973\t\n974\t xml\n975\t\n976\t .\n977\t\n978\t## Instructions for reporting errors\n979\t\n980\tWe are continuing to improve HTML versions of papers, and your feedback helps enhance accessibility and mobile\n981\t support. To report errors in the HTML that will help us improve conversion and rendering, choose any of the\n982\t methods listed below:\n983\t\n984\t- Click the